# openastroara user gets passwordless sudo for one specific script only.
# Validated by `visudo -cf` during package build per §34.3.
#
# configure-storage.sh — invoked by the storage-config flow (§29.1.4)
#
# NOTE: the openastroara-server unit sets NoNewPrivileges=true, under which sudo
# (setuid) refuses to run, so the line below is not reachable from the packaged
# daemon. Storage goes through openastroara-storage@.service + a polkit rule
# (usr/share/polkit-1/rules.d/50-openastroara-storage.rules); the daemon only
# falls back to this sudo line on a dev rig that has no packaged unit. Guider
# unit control and the §33 update push (#1122, openastroara-update@.service)
# are likewise polkit rules, with no sudo fallback at all.
#
# Mode 0440, owned by root:root, as Debian sudoers requires.
# Keep env_reset (the default) on this entry: configure-storage.sh honours an FSTAB_LOCK
# override and its wrapper storage-request.sh honours DIR/HELPER (for the daemon's tests,
# #1135); a SETENV/env_keep here would let the daemon user steer root to paths of its
# choosing.
openastroara ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /opt/openastroara/scripts/configure-storage.sh
